\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Ordinary real determinants of isotypic blocks}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In \ref{fdip-0055} every determinant is the determinant of a real
linear operator. The multiplicity matrix #{Q_\Xi} contributes through
left multiplication on #{D_\Xi^{m_\Xi}}, and the sector determinant
is that real determinant raised to #{r_\Xi=\dim_{D_\Xi}W_\Xi}. When
#{D_\Xi=\mathbb H} this is still the real determinant of a real
operator of dimension #{4m_\Xi}, not a quaternion-valued determinant.
The eigenvalue form is the one recorded for \ref{fdip-0050}.}
